                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "2be0dd47-9acc-4976-82d4-ce97954f4733",
                        "entry_id": "5d892e49-95d6-3c66-b270-5d28edd60d82",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural",
                            "feminine"
                        ],
                        "form": "timorées"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "c950cf46-4302-341a-b34b-900ffba08556",
                        "entry_id": "5d892e49-95d6-3c66-b270-5d28edd60d82",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Qui est trop disposé à la crainte, au scrupule."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "4bff447f-eb0b-47ca-9f23-615115ada71d",
                                "sense_id": "c950cf46-4302-341a-b34b-900ffba08556",
                                "text": "Sous les gouvernements faibles et timorés, qui se piquaient de pratiquer l'alliance du trône et de l'autel, c'est l'Église qui s'est prévalue du Concordat pour assurer sa prépondérance, …."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "eff3dccc-a7a3-4765-a37f-5b499f9a5cf6",
                                "sense_id": "c950cf46-4302-341a-b34b-900ffba08556",
                                "text": "Il est extraordinairement timoré. « C’est le lièvre de La Fontaine », disait mon père. Il ajoutait : « L’ombre de ses oreilles l’épouvante »."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "32da76a7-0692-4d77-8807-153f20cf1f99",
                                "sense_id": "c950cf46-4302-341a-b34b-900ffba08556",
                                "text": "L’appui timoré de Justin Trudeau à la France suscite ce type de questionnement à la veille de l’ouverture du procès en Cour supérieure qui devra statuer sur la validité de la loi québécoise sur la laïcité."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "f7e998a8-0ea6-3ea1-ad82-285b70decf4b",
                        "entry_id": "5d892e49-95d6-3c66-b270-5d28edd60d82",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Qui a peur dans une situation particulière."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "5fa49676-88ac-4465-9017-dbc3930b1b7a",
                                "sense_id": "f7e998a8-0ea6-3ea1-ad82-285b70decf4b",
                                "text": "Mais comment partager notre vécu ? Nous sommes trop souvent timorés. Nous craignons que les autres nous traitent de naïfs !"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "af1c268f-a174-4aa4-83d9-59b3666e5dbf",
                                "sense_id": "f7e998a8-0ea6-3ea1-ad82-285b70decf4b",
                                "text": "Grâce à Niclas Füllkrug, en toute fin de match, les hommes d’Hansi Flick ont évité le pire face à des Espagnols timorés (1-1)."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "15943d38-0d98-4584-bff9-d4c895d0975e",
                        "source_entry_id": "5d892e49-95d6-3c66-b270-5d28edd60d82",
                        "target_lang_word": "timorous",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "timorous",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5f3ccf71-4294-3069-92bc-93d3ef8d6f2a",
                                        "entry_id": "0b1d02e9-ebf0-360b-8c11-baf84e4df22b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Tending to be easily frightened; shy, timid."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3e27c1f0-e856-4d34-9ed0-ad88984356da",
                                                "sense_id": "5f3ccf71-4294-3069-92bc-93d3ef8d6f2a",
                                                "text": "But thou now O temerous ⁊ weake ſely ſhepe, thynke yt ſufficient for thee, onely to walke after me, which am thy ſhepehearde ⁊ gouernor: […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1635b258-bc79-4c31-84aa-043c1b8363a7",
                                                "sense_id": "5f3ccf71-4294-3069-92bc-93d3ef8d6f2a",
                                                "text": "Thys faute of puſillanimitye and tymorous mynde, letteth a man alſo mani tymes from the doynge of manye good thynges, whyche (if he tooke a good ſtomake to hym in the truſt of Gods helpe) he were wel able to do."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b8c23467-5c91-4c35-9cff-2a1ee631adf0",
                                                "sense_id": "5f3ccf71-4294-3069-92bc-93d3ef8d6f2a",
                                                "text": "[T]hey might thank themſelves onely, & their ovvn timerous conceits & imaginations, that ſuch things vvere ſo dread & terrible."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "634c6705-9cbe-4076-ad50-f77784db5877",
                                                "sense_id": "5f3ccf71-4294-3069-92bc-93d3ef8d6f2a",
                                                "text": "[I]n the ſtudy of the reign of Theodoſius [I], vve are reduced to illuſtrate the partial narrative of Zoſimus, by the obſcure hints of fragments and chronicles, by the figurative ſtyle of poetry or panegyric, and by the precarious aſſiſtance of the eccleſiaſtical vvriters, vvho, in the heat of religious faction, are apt to deſpiſe the profane virtues of ſincerity and moderation. Conſcious of theſe diſadvantages, vvhich vvill continue to involve a conſiderable portion of the decline and fall of the Roman empire, I ſhall proceed vvith doubtful and timorous ſteps."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "941eff60-af85-4c5f-9f2e-157a76f2663f",
                                                "sense_id": "5f3ccf71-4294-3069-92bc-93d3ef8d6f2a",
                                                "text": "VVee ſleekit, covvrin, tim'rous beaſtie, / Oh, vvhat a panic's in thy breaſtie!"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "47f8b1d6-4cb3-472e-8f48-785bbaf18b65",
                                                "sense_id": "5f3ccf71-4294-3069-92bc-93d3ef8d6f2a",
                                                "text": "Animals of the hare kind, like all others that feed entirely upon vegetables, are inoffenſive and timorous. As Nature furniſhes them vvith a moſt abundant ſupply, they have not that rapacity after food remarkable in ſuch as are often ſtinted in their proviſion."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "327cb77a-a5cf-4824-b766-7f0607926837",
                                                "sense_id": "5f3ccf71-4294-3069-92bc-93d3ef8d6f2a",
                                                "text": "His troops murmured at this timorous policy, and the people of the south, on whom the charges of the expeditions fell with peculiar heaviness, from their neighbourhood to the scene of the operations, complained that \"the war was carried on against them, not against the infidel.\""
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2b1d5a48-3291-499b-9ba5-3bc915f20274",
                                                "sense_id": "5f3ccf71-4294-3069-92bc-93d3ef8d6f2a",
                                                "text": "[I]n his later years, he [James II of England] repeatedly, at conjunctures such as have often inspired timorous and delicate women with heroic courage, showed a pusillanimous anxiety about his personal safety."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5a7e15f5-726d-4153-926c-0cde82b59dfc",
                                                "sense_id": "5f3ccf71-4294-3069-92bc-93d3ef8d6f2a",
                                                "text": "[H]e was one of those weak creatures full of a shifty cunning—who face neither God nor man, who face not even themselves, void of pride, timorous, anæmic, hateful souls."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ff91de61-bb90-463c-82f5-2f73b8d847ad",
                                                "sense_id": "5f3ccf71-4294-3069-92bc-93d3ef8d6f2a",
                                                "text": "\"Upon my word,\" said Micky, \"only I was timorous i' puttin' the good people to too much throuble, I was on the point i' mentionin' the same meself.\""
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7161084f-5cbf-428d-b9f5-97bf9f4aede1",
                                                "sense_id": "5f3ccf71-4294-3069-92bc-93d3ef8d6f2a",
                                                "text": "He turned a long you are wrong gaze on Stephen of timorous dark pride at the soft impeachment, with a glance also of entreaty for he seemed to glean in a kind of a way that it wasn't all exactly …"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3dfd498a-a029-45fe-9283-75daee9c8569",
                                                "sense_id": "5f3ccf71-4294-3069-92bc-93d3ef8d6f2a",
                                                "text": "The suspect was a man of forty, with a grey, timorous face, dressed only in a ragged longyi kilted to the knee, beneath which his lank, curved shins were specked with tick-bites."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b3d28792-7cee-3038-894b-ef0eb68123ce",
                                        "entry_id": "0b1d02e9-ebf0-360b-8c11-baf84e4df22b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Feeling fear; afraid, fearful, frightened."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "archaic"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "865f3bac-01a3-461b-a1fa-3edb245042ec",
                                                "sense_id": "b3d28792-7cee-3038-894b-ef0eb68123ce",
                                                "text": "He [the Devil] marketh well […] mennes complexions within thẽ [them], health, or ſicknes, good humours or badde, by which they be light hearted or lumpiſh, ſtrong hearted, or faynt & fieble of ſpirite, bolde and hardy, or timorous and fearefull of courage."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2d0ea0b0-3fd9-436e-94fd-98b44b134715",
                                                "sense_id": "b3d28792-7cee-3038-894b-ef0eb68123ce",
                                                "text": "Men call her Athliot: vvho cannot be / More vvretched made by infelicitie, / Vnleſſe ſhe here had an immortall breath / Or liuing thus, liu'd timerous of death."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "924702eb-bb97-4a5c-b65e-a821662d2393",
                                                "sense_id": "b3d28792-7cee-3038-894b-ef0eb68123ce",
                                                "text": "VVeaker I am, vvoe is mee, and vvorſe then you, / You have not ſinn'd, nor need be timorous, […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "97283198-2c24-43ac-a04c-9ea748308f06",
                                                "sense_id": "b3d28792-7cee-3038-894b-ef0eb68123ce",
                                                "text": "Remember, my ſon, that human life is the journey of a day. […] VVe approach them [the gardens of pleasure] vvith ſcruple and heſitation; vve enter them, but enter timorous and trembling; and alvvays hope to paſs through them vvithout loſing the road of virtue, vvhich vve for a vvhile keep in our ſight, and to vvhich vve propoſe to return."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e20e51d0-2693-4d85-a73a-79f21d697397",
                                                "sense_id": "b3d28792-7cee-3038-894b-ef0eb68123ce",
                                                "text": "[H]e had none of his old cronies to \"tackle,\" and was rather timorous on venturing on Joe; […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "655adba1-7836-362d-9caa-100b6f5eb8b5",
                                        "entry_id": "0b1d02e9-ebf0-360b-8c11-baf84e4df22b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Fastidious in dressing."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "UK",
                                            "dialectal"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8c91bbae-9421-34ca-a55f-53c7c77a672c",
                                        "entry_id": "0b1d02e9-ebf0-360b-8c11-baf84e4df22b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Fired with intense feeling; passionate."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "UK",
                                            "dialectal"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9fb60a8e-2b1b-313b-a032-94d123c65b6c",
                                        "entry_id": "0b1d02e9-ebf0-360b-8c11-baf84e4df22b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Hard to manage; difficult, tiresome."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "UK",
                                            "dialectal"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9b428011-dce0-3c7c-95c3-d5a7cc740f5f",
                                        "entry_id": "0b1d02e9-ebf0-360b-8c11-baf84e4df22b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Causing dread or fear; dreadful, terrible."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2477996f-6edb-4d9e-ab64-8129ce9712aa",
                                                "sense_id": "9b428011-dce0-3c7c-95c3-d5a7cc740f5f",
                                                "text": "Well, having past halfe way downewards, wee came to the most scurrile and timorous Discent of the whole passage, where with much difficuty, I set safe the foure Germanes in our narrow Rode hewen out of the craggy Hill; […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e949c80f-7ad3-385e-bbd0-c713b90002a9",
                                        "entry_id": "0b1d02e9-ebf0-360b-8c11-baf84e4df22b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Humble, modest; also, showing reverence; respectful, reverent, reverential."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "dc27a319-0d0c-4045-aff1-90c27535fae4",
                        "source_entry_id": "5d892e49-95d6-3c66-b270-5d28edd60d82",
                        "target_lang_word": "angstig",
                        "target_lang_code": "nl",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "angstig",
                                "target_lang_code": "nl",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "719a22be-fe71-3266-af2d-5e02b31e338b",
                                        "entry_id": "d624cf42-a1fe-3237-81e5-c5a3f443cb54",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "vol van bange gevoelens"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "06a65042-56e2-47dd-b38e-17b0a1889569",
                                                "sense_id": "719a22be-fe71-3266-af2d-5e02b31e338b",
                                                "text": "We hebben zo iets angstigs beleefd! We werden bijna door een grote vrachtauto van de weg gedrukt."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "05d7598f-98eb-4c83-9bd9-92597c2b408d",
                                                "sense_id": "719a22be-fe71-3266-af2d-5e02b31e338b",
                                                "text": "Ondertussen was ik stukje bij beetje uit mijn angstige gemoedstoestand van de afgelopen weken gekomen en voelde ik me steeds beter op de trail."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dda02fa7-c8c5-4ccf-9555-2b0185e8d23f",
                                                "sense_id": "719a22be-fe71-3266-af2d-5e02b31e338b",
                                                "text": "Hij stak beide, gesloten handen omhoog en keek gemaakt angstig."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "e889bb26-9c80-4ec6-b5cc-74167413ef22",
                        "source_entry_id": "5d892e49-95d6-3c66-b270-5d28edd60d82",
                        "target_lang_word": "achterdochtig",
                        "target_lang_code": "nl",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "achterdochtig",
                                "target_lang_code": "nl",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4b5e89db-92fa-330d-83a5-d86a8c66d22d",
                                        "entry_id": "7cd04b50-5c2d-3464-a111-829f87c5bb56",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "geneigd verdenking te koesteren"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4151ef76-ddb0-435b-ae1d-a97b57ffc2c4",
                                                "sense_id": "4b5e89db-92fa-330d-83a5-d86a8c66d22d",
                                                "text": "Hij is de achterdochtigste kerel die ik ken."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3eee70e4-4d43-4934-8f6c-25aff1b229a4",
                                                "sense_id": "4b5e89db-92fa-330d-83a5-d86a8c66d22d",
                                                "text": "Iemand die ziekelijk achterdochtig is noemen we paranoïde."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b0aaaa9b-0dee-4bde-bc1e-6192de158cdf",
                                                "sense_id": "4b5e89db-92fa-330d-83a5-d86a8c66d22d",
                                                "text": "Sarah glimlachte. 'Verstandig. Volgens mij zou iedereen een stuk gelukkiger zijn als we allemaal waren zoals u. Ik kom wel naar u toe. Je weet nooit precies wanneer Harold thuis is, en ik wil niet dat hij achterdochtig wordt.'"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ca37bbc6-46ed-4e11-bc78-17bfb6c735a0",
                                                "sense_id": "4b5e89db-92fa-330d-83a5-d86a8c66d22d",
                                                "text": "' Als mensen gaan vertellen hoe geweldig hun partner is, word ik altijd wat achterdochtig."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "1eb7397f-f113-42eb-a452-1323943a94df",
                        "source_entry_id": "5d892e49-95d6-3c66-b270-5d28edd60d82",
